{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/feedbackArcSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/feedbackarcset()"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"feedbackArcSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The heuristic orders the vertices in a sequence and takes every edge that points leftward","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in it, and every self-loop. It repeatedly removes a sink (placed at the right end of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence), else a source (at the left end), else the vertex whose out-degree minus","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in-degree is largest (at the left end), with the least ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" offset on ties. Sinks and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sources are removed in the order they became one, starting from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Self-loops do not count toward degrees; parallel edges count once each. On an acyclic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph the result is empty, and for every graph, removing (or reversing) the returned edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves no directed cycle.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Eades, Lin and Smyth, “A fast and effective heuristic for the feedback arc set problem”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Information Processing Letters 47(6), 1993. The largest-difference vertices are kept in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary heap so that ties go to the least offset."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O((n + m) log n) time, O(n + m) memory.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles","doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The edges that Eades, Lin and Smyth’s greedy heuristic removes to make the graph acyclic,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":", ascending: a feedback arc set, small in practice but not minimum.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Every self-loop is in it: arcs 0 → 0, 0 → 1, 1 → 0 give positions [0, 2].","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6CyclesE14feedbackArcSetSay5Edges_5IndexQZGyF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Cycles","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"feedbackArcSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"FeedbackArcSet.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cycles\/FeedbackArcSet.swift#L23"},"title":"feedbackArcSet()","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"references":{"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles":{"url":"\/documentation\/cycles","title":"Cycles","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/feedbackArcSet()":{"abstract":[{"text":"The edges that Eades, Lin and Smyth’s greedy heuristic removes to make the graph acyclic,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ascending: a feedback arc set, small in practice but not minimum.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Every self-loop is in it: arcs 0 → 0, 0 → 1, 1 → 0 give positions [0, 2].","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/feedbackarcset()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/feedbackArcSet()","title":"feedbackArcSet()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"feedbackArcSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0